WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:04.700
Now that the movie's in theaters, Birds of
Prey fans can finally dig into the film's

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:08.320
massive ensemble, twisted set pieces, and
inventive action.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:12.900
With so much going on, it can be easy to miss
all the plot developments or know where everyone

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:13.960
stands by the end.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.200
We're here to help.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:17.040
"We're gonna have to work together."

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:22.860
Birds of Prey's subtitle touts the film as
the story of Harley Quinn's "fantabulous emancipation,"

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:23.380
and it is.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:28.340
Harley starts the film as an emotional wreck
prone to binge drinking, crying jags, and

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:29.780
blowing up chemical plants.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:34.360
That all changes when she gains a chance to
earn her freedom from her bad reputation and

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:36.780
bonds with the rest of the Birds of Prey team.

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:41.960
By the end of the film, she's got a new protege
in Cassandra Cain, a new probably-not-legal

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:45.800
business and a new reputation as someone who
can get things done.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:50.879
But the grenade-explosion death of Roman Sionis
doesn't necessarily mean all of Harley's trouble

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:52.120
is about to go away.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:57.040
She used to roll with the Joker, after all,
and no matter how far she gets from that relationship

00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:00.940
there's someone, somewhere, looking to cause
her pain for her past sins.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:05.020
Harley is smart enough to know this, and she'll
no doubt be looking over her shoulder for

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:06.140
the next great threat.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:11.560
When we first meet Cassandra Cain, she's a
low-level pickpocket who wanders the streets

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:16.020
of Gotham trying to avoid going back to the
crappy apartment where her parents are constantly

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:16.520
fighting.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:20.960
Over the course of the film, she goes on a
massive adventure, becomes the focus of a

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:25.260
citywide scavenger hunt, and finds a new big
sister figure in the form of Harley Quinn.

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:28.740
Cassandra's got a whole new life ahead of
her as Harley's protege.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.000
What does she do now?

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:34.440
The possibilities seem endless, considering
who she's hanging out with, but one path seems

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:35.440
very likely.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:39.720
Yes, the film version of Cassandra is very
different from the comics, but we do know

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:42.920
that comics Cassandra took on the role of
Batgirl for a while.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:47.640
It would take a few years and a little training,
but perhaps movie Cassandra could also pull

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:48.200
that off.

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:53.920
Detective Renee Montoya starts the film as
a rough-edged, determined, smart Gotham City

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:58.500
cop with a tendency toward alcoholism and
deep resentment toward her mostly-male colleagues

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:00.440
for taking promotions she deserved.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:05.060
By the end, she's not exactly a new woman,
but she does seem to have renewed purpose.

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:09.310
The vigilante life will allow her to do the
kind of good in Gotham that she never could

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:09.980
with a badge.

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:15.260
Renee becomes a founding member of the Birds
of Prey alongside her new friends Helena Bertinelli

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:18.730
and Dinah Lance,
cementing her place as a crime fighter outside

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:19.780
the realm of the law.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:24.480
Her old cop connections will no doubt make
her very good at that job, but it's not necessarily

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.000
the end of Renee's evolution.

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:31.700
Longtime DC Comics readers know Renee eventually
became the new incarnation of masked vigilante

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:35.260
the Question, a transition we could still
see on the big screen someday.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:37.760
Black Canary is something of a mystery.

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:42.300
When we meet her, she's a lounge singer at
Black Mask's club, doing whatever she can

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.080
to get by.

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:47.820
But then she displays tremendous fighting
abilities as well as her supersonic "Canary

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:51.440
Cry," which lets us all know that she's got
gifts she's been keeping under wraps.

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:56.480
What the film doesn't tell us is how and why
Canary is so gifted, which means her backstory

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:59.060
is ripe for exploration in future films.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:03.620
With Canary now one of Gotham City's most
visible vigilantes, and there's nowhere to

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:04.140
go but up.

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:08.600
In upcoming films, we could certainly see
her comic book love interest Green Arrow one

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:12.810
day, though a version of the Canary/Arrow
dynamic did just recently play out on the

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:14.350
small screen for eight seasons.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:20.430
Helena Bertinelli seems like the most straightforward
character in the title team, because she seems

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:25.430
to have only one real motivation: Avenge the
deaths of her family members by killing everyone

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:26.020
tied to it.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:30.790
When she finally kills the last person she
believes to be involved in the massacre, Victor

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:33.960
Zsasz, Helena has to find something else to
live for.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:38.020
"Psychologically speaking, vengeance rarely
brings the catharsis we hope for."

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:42.130
By the end of the film, Helena may not have
shed any of the leftover awkwardness from

00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:46.569
her single-minded pursuits as the Huntress,
but she has gained a broader perspective of

00:03:46.569 --> 00:03:47.120
the world.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:51.720
As Renee Montoya noted, she's fooling herself
if she thinks the symptoms of the problem

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:54.700
that killed her family stopped with the last
name on her list.

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:59.280
Now, as a member of the Birds of Prey, she
has a new outlet for making the world a better

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:04.240
place, and stopping the deaths of other families
in the process, using her regained inheritance

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:05.980
to fund the whole operation.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:12.680
Birds of Prey sets up Roman Sionis, a.k.a.
Black Mask, as a true Big Bad worthy of Harley's

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:13.180
fear.

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:17.740
Roman is a truly terrifying, unhinged mob
boss who seems to have bought and killed his

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:22.140
way to the top, to the point that by the end
of the film, he basically has an army at his

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:22.900
beck and call.

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:27.010
Plus, we know that a lot of what he's done
in the past means very few mob leaders are

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:31.020
fit to challenge him, and those that do find
themselves without faces.

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:35.280
But by the end of the film, Gotham's most
powerful mob boss has been blown to bits on

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:36.360
Founders Pier.

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:41.060
His right-hand man is also dead, and there's
suddenly a very prominent power vacuum in

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:42.070
Gotham's underworld.

00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:44.600
So, who's going to rise up and fill that void?

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:48.680
There are a lot of candidates who could step
up, particularly with the Joker seemingly

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:49.800
out of the picture.

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:53.960
Perhaps it's time for the Penguin to become
the big-screen crime lord we've all been waiting

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:54.560
to see.

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:59.740
Much like the Joker, Batman doesn't appear
in Birds of Prey, but his presence is felt

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:00.400
nonetheless.

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:05.350
Harley references him as part of her origin
story, noting he arrested her after she helped

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:07.360
Joker break out of Arkham Asylum.

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:11.660
He's often either the butt of Harley's jokes
or serves as a reminder that Harley still

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:13.240
remembers her encounters with him.

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:15.420
He's also brought up in subtler ways.

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:20.280
For one thing, Harley Quinn's pet hyena is
named Bruce, and she's so proud of that name

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:22.340
that she wears it on a chain around her neck.

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:25.000
He's named after billionaire playboy Bruce
Wayne...

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:28.400
"I named him Bruce after that hunky Wayne
guy."

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:31.180
...so does Harley know that Bruce Wayne is
Batman?

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:35.880
Then there's the post-credits audio snippet,
in which Harley promises to tell us a secret.

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:39.880
She gets as far as saying "Batman f-" before
the audio cuts out.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:44.060
Given her hyena's name could one assume Harley
is sweet on the Batman?

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:46.560
We may never know, but it's fun to think about.

